[
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">SyntaxNodeKind</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- error:</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">(kernel) application type mismatch</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  Array.map Sigma.fst</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">argument has type</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  (n : Nat) × Green n → Nat</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">but function has type</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  (_nested.Sigma_2 → Nat) → Array _nested.Sigma_2 → Array Nat</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">token</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">kind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SyntaxNodeKind</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">node</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">kind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SyntaxNodeKind</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">children</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Array</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">Σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">Green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">children</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Sigma</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Hi all!<br>\nI'm trying to create intrinsically well-formed green trees which contain their widths in their type. As I understand, nested inductive types are elaborated by creating a temporary mutual block, with the nested inductive specialised. So in this case, the nested Sigma Nat Green would turn into a temporary _nested.Sigma_2. However, I can't do operations on it, like project the .fst of the sigma, because _nested.Sigma_2 bears no relationship to the actual \"Sigma\". Is this intentional, and is there a different way to achieve this?</p>",
        "id": 577563219,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Chen",
        "timestamp": 1772732750
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That looks like a bug somewhere, these <code>_nested</code> names should not leak like that. I would under what circumstances that happens. It could be that that data type is simply not supported, though, and only the error message needs to be better.</p>",
        "id": 577605942,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1772747945
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hmm, I'm sure we don't support mentioning the current inductive types in the index of the constrictors' result type. But Sigma is mentioned in the type argument of <a href=\"http://Array.map\">Array.map</a> . So this is not supported. Probably it's even an instance of induction-recursion or something wild like that.</p>",
        "id": 577606647,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1772748235
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I could see how this could be interpreted as some sneaky induction-recursion</p>",
        "id": 577607350,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Chen",
        "timestamp": 1772748521
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And induction-recursion is exactly what I was trying to avoid by writing it this way</p>",
        "id": 577607409,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Chen",
        "timestamp": 1772748543
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>FWIW, I am aware it is possible to write this using mutual inductives like</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">mutual</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">token</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">kind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SyntaxNodeKind</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">node</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">kind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SyntaxNodeKind</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">children</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GreenList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GreenList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nil</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GreenList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cons</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">head</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tail</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GreenList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GreenList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>But then you lose the benefits of <code>Array</code>.</p>",
        "id": 577607792,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Chen",
        "timestamp": 1772748723
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Right. But the big difference here is that there are no functions over the newly defined typs occurring in the index of your constructors.<br>\nI wager you could have an inductive <code>Vec</code> and successfully nest through that.</p>",
        "id": 577607970,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1772748805
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, you mean</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Vec</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nil</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Vec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cons</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">head</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tail</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Vec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Vec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">token</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">kind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SyntaxNodeKind</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">node</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">kind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SyntaxNodeKind</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">children</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Vec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 577609190,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Chen",
        "timestamp": 1772749378
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In case other people come across this and are keen on (some kind) of a solution to induction-recursion, I'll leave a note to my other thread where <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/multiple.20universe.20mutual.20inductives/near/626492716\">I offer support</a> for it.</p>",
        "id": 626494980,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Meiburg",
        "timestamp": 1790217504
    }
]